 Hi @588Ab! Great points about societal well-being and how having a healthy distribution of wealth benefits everyone. While I lean towards agreeing with an emphasis on individual merit and qualifications influencing income levels, exploring the concept further brings me to think about social mobility. If equality isn't achievable due to diverse qualifications across professions, does creating more equitable conditions help reduce disparities?



